---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import { site, mailLink, waLink } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout title="How to order custom labels and stickers" description={`The ordering process from specification to delivery: what to send, how proofs work, sample policy, payment and shipping. Minimum ${site.moq} units.`}>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "How to order" }]} />
  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap narrow prose">
      <h1>How to order</h1>
      <p class="lead" style="font-size:1.08rem;color:var(--ink-2)">
        Four steps from an idea to a delivered box. No account, no cart, no automated pricing — a person checks
        the specification and quotes it.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Send your specification</h2>
      <p>Email or WhatsApp is enough. What we need to quote accurately:</p>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Product type</th><td>Label or sticker; roll or sheet</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Size and shape</th><td>Width × height in mm, diameter, or a dieline for irregular shapes</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Material preference</th><td>Paper, PP, PET, vinyl, clear — or ask for a recommendation</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Quantity</th><td>Per design; multiple designs are fine if material and size match</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Finishing</th><td>Gloss, matte, laminate, foil — optional</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Destination</th><td>Country and postcode, for the shipping line</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Artwork</th><td>Vector file if you have one; not required for a first quote</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>2. Quotation</h2>
      <p>
        We confirm what is producible at your quantity, flag anything that will not work (a 2 mm text on a matte
        uncoated stock, a white logo on clear vinyl without a white backing layer), and quote the job.
        Quotations normally go out within one working day and state the unit price, setup, shipping and lead time.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Artwork approval and sample</h2>
      <p>
        A digital proof is always included and must be approved in writing before production. If you want to see
        and feel the material first, a physical sample can be produced — useful when the label has to survive
        condensation, oil or a curved jar.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/artwork-guidelines/">Artwork guidelines</a> covers file formats, bleed, colour and resolution.</p>

      <h2>4. Production and delivery</h2>
      <p>
        Production typically takes 7–12 working days after artwork approval. Shipping is quoted with the order:
        express courier for small runs, air or sea freight for larger ones. Tracking is provided, and duties or
        import taxes are explained before you confirm rather than on delivery.
      </p>

      <h2>Payment</h2>
      <p>
        Payment terms are confirmed with the quotation. Production starts after the deposit clears and the proof is
        approved; the balance is due before dispatch. We do not take card details through this website.
      </p>

      <h2>What we need from you, in one line</h2>
      <p><strong>Size · quantity · material (or “recommend one”) · destination · artwork or reference photo.</strong></p>
      <p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={mailLink("New order — specification")}>Email the specification</a>
        <a class="btn btn-wa" href={waLink("Hello, I would like to order custom labels or stickers.\n\nProduct:\nSize:\nQuantity:\nDestination:")} rel="noopener">Send on WhatsApp</a>
      </p>

      <p class="small">Minimum order: {site.moq} units per design. Lead time: {site.leadTime}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CtaBand />
</BaseLayout>
